# Rank 1686 / CVE-2024-39124: the Roundup classhelper popups rendered the
# `property` and `form` query parameters into a `<script>` element through a
# ZPT `tal:content` whose expression carried the `structure` modifier, so the
# interpolated values reached the page unescaped and a crafted
# `?@template=help&property=</script><script>...` URL executed in the popup
# (CWE-79). `structure` is ZPT's documented "emit the result without HTML
# quoting" switch; the fixed revision drops it and leaves the interpolation alone, so
# the discriminating fact is the modifier, not any value. The fixing commit commit
# 860e3c8d0 remediates exactly this CVE in 24 template lines across the five
# shipped tracker templates plus website/issues; the same commit's
# roundup/cgi/client.py hunks belong to CVE-2024-39125 (Referer reflected
# through an unescaped error message) and CVE-2024-39126 (Content-Security-
# Policy on downloads), so the pool row's `python` language field names the
# repository, not the file the fixed revision lands in. No row correction: repo, CVE
# and commit are all correct.
#
# ATTENTION, template-attribute value spans lines -- the whole weakness lives
# in `tal:content="structure string:..."` attribute values, which no `.html`
# route reads as a unit. The JavaScript frontend extracts only the bytes
# between `<script>` and `</script>` (`htmlScriptSource`,
# internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/javascript.go:207) and the element is
# empty here because the generated script *is* the attribute value; the
# config frontend's `.html` paths are `scanHTMLReferrerLinks` and the
# `config_text_template_*` scopes, and `scanTextTemplate`
# (internal/extract/frontend/config/config.go:312) evaluates every rule
# against one trimmed line, as does `scanTemplateExpressions` at :378 for the
# jelly/jsp scopes -- its only cross-line state is a sticky `escapeActive`
# flag and a variable-alias set. Roundup's own layout puts the `structure
# string:` opener and the `${request/form/...}` interpolation two to three
# lines apart, so "raw string expression that interpolates a request path"
# is not expressible. Measured on the real templates, three runs each side:
# a `tal` scope with the line needle `structure string:` reports 36 findings
# at the parent and still 14 at the fixed revision -- 10 on page.html's
# `string:$m <br/>` message renders, 2 on milestone.item.html's
# `string:Created on`, and 2 on the static `<script>` bodies the fixed revision itself
# split out of _generic.help-submit.html, which carry no interpolation at
# all, so the binding would flag lines the remediation wrote; narrowing the
# needle to `structure string:<!--` (the legacy script-hiding idiom) gives a
# clean 14 -> 0 but catches only 14 of the 24 vulnerable instances -- the
# same weakness written without the comment idiom, as roundup's own calendar
# and help templates are, walks past it, which is the repro-shape test and
# not a binding worth keeping. Nothing is labelled on the real files today:
# `vyql match` on the classhelper template reports no source, sink or
# control, and the unmodified scanner reports 25 VYQL-INJ-028 rows on this
# tree at both revisions, all of them the jinja2 family's `|safe` filters,
# identical before and after. No definition change shipped. Spec
# cve_rank1686 records the classhelper script block unescaped, escaped, and
# the ordinary `structure context/.../field` widget form, all asserting
# reject VYQL-INJ-028: when template attribute values are extracted as a
# unit, the first must flip to expect and the other two must not.

test "rank1686: a classhelper popup renders request parameters into a script element with the structure modifier"
  lang config
  file _generic.help.html
  reject VYQL-INJ-028
  code
  ```
  <html tal:define="property request/form/property/value | nothing">
    <head>
      <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="@@file/style.css" />
      <tal:block tal:condition="python:'property' in request.form">
      <title><tal:x tal:content="property | default" i18n:translate="" /> help</title>
      <script language="Javascript" type="text/javascript"
          tal:content="structure string:
          // this is the name of the field in the original form that we're working on
          form  = window.opener.document.${request/form/form/value};
          field  = '${request/form/property/value}';">
      </script>
      </tal:block>
    </head>
   <body class="body" onload="resetList();">
   <form name="frm_help" tal:attributes="action request/base"
         tal:define="props python:request.form['properties'].value.split(',')">
     <input type="text" name="text_preview" size="24" class="preview"
            onchange="reviseList(this.value);"/>
   </form>
   </body>
  </html>
  ```

test "rank1686: the classhelper popup escapes the interpolated script block"
  lang config
  file _generic.help.html
  reject VYQL-INJ-028
  code
  ```
  <html tal:define="property request/form/property/value | nothing">
    <head>
      <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="@@file/style.css" />
      <tal:block tal:condition="python:'property' in request.form">
      <title><tal:x tal:content="property | default" i18n:translate="" /> help</title>
      <script language="Javascript" type="text/javascript"
          tal:content="string:
          // this is the name of the field in the original form that we're working on
          form  = window.opener.document.${request/form/form/value};
          field  = '${request/form/property/value}';">
      </script>
      </tal:block>
    </head>
   <body class="body" onload="resetList();">
   <form name="frm_help" tal:attributes="action request/base"
         tal:define="props python:request.form['properties'].value.split(',')">
     <input type="text" name="text_preview" size="24" class="preview"
            onchange="reviseList(this.value);"/>
   </form>
   </body>
  </html>
  ```

test "rank1686: a helper that hands a built field widget through keeps the structure modifier"
  lang config
  file user.register.html
  reject VYQL-INJ-028
  code
  ```
  <html tal:define="property request/form/property/value | nothing">
    <head>
      <title>Register</title>
    </head>
   <body class="body">
   <form method="POST" name="itemSynopsis"
         tal:attributes="action context/designator">
   <table class="form">
    <tr>
     <th i18n:translate="">Username</th>
     <td tal:content="structure context/username/field">username</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
     <th i18n:translate="">Password</th>
     <td tal:content="structure context/password/field">password</td>
    </tr>
   </table>
   </form>
   </body>
  </html>
  ```
